" Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Gerunds and Infinitives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When a verb ends with -ing (doing \u2013 enjoying - reacting), is a <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span>. An <span class=\"strong\">infinitive</span> is formed with \u201cto + verb\u201d (to do \u2013 to divide \u2013 to decide). <br> There are rules about which verbs you can use with <span class=\"strong\">gerunds</span>and which can use with <span class=\"strong\">infinitives</span>. <br> Take into account that the <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span>can be used as the subject of the sentence. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Followed by a <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span>:<br/><br/>  Verbs that express <span class=\"strong\">likes</span>/<span class=\"strong\">dislikes</span>:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">like<br/> love<br/> enjoy<br/> hate</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Example:  <br/> I <span class=\"strong\">enjoy having</span> a lucky rabbit's foot.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">like</span>/<span class=\"italic\">love</span>/<span class=\"italic\">hate</span> can also be followed by an infinitive.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Followed by an <span class=\"strong\">infinitive</span>:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\"> hope<br/> seem<br/> decide<br/> start</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "  Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">  I <span class=\"strong\">decided to buy</span> a good luck charm.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">infinitives </span>after <span class=\"strong\">adjectives</span>. <br/>Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I was <span class=\"strong\">happy to write</span> about a lucky penny I found.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " An activity can be used as a <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span>-  this <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span> is the subject of the sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Keeping</span> a lucky charm is important.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Being lucky</span> is always nice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Reading this letter reminds me that I am a very lucky person. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I really wanted to travel. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Conditional Sentences with <span class=\"italic\">If</span> Clause", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the first conditional to say it's possible that you will or will not do something. In that condition, something else may, may not, will or will not happen.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The parts of the sentence are divided into two clauses: the <span class=\"italic\">if</span> clause and the <span class=\"italic\">condition</span> clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the second conditional to talk about hypothetical situations. There is no certainty that the condition will be fulfilled. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"> If I had a million dollars, I would travel to Europe</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Do you have a million dollars?  No.<br/> Is it possible to suddenly get a million dollars? Not really.<br/> What would you do if you had a million dollars? Travel to Europe.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " You use the  <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past verb</span> +  <span class=\"strong\"> <span class=\"italic\">would</span></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"First Conditional: 1st Clause\\t\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"First Conditional: 2nd Clause\\t\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If I study today,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'll go to the party tonight.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible that I can go to the party tonight, but only if I study first. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Second Conditional:<br/>If ... + Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Second Conditional: <br/>would + base verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> If I won the lottery,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I would travel to Europe.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It is an impossible situation because it is unlikely to win the lottery and therefore can only happen in a hypothetical situation.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "If I won the lottery, I would travel there first. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If I were lucky enough, it would be the first thing that I would do. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If I had a lot of money, I would buy some pumpkins and give them to a charity.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If I were you, I would not make fun of your friends' superstitions.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rabbit's foot", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the foot of a rabbit carried as a good luck charm", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: For luck, I always keep a rabbit's foot in my pocket when I write a test.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about superstitions.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "horseshoe", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a U-shaped metal plate nailed to a horse's hoof to protect it from injuries", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I heard that a horseshoe brings good luck.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ridiculous", "type": "name"}, {"content": "\u200bstupid or \u200bunreasonable; laughable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Some people think it is ridiculous to believe in good luck.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "good luck charm", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something believed to bring good luck", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She kept a penny in her shoe as a good luck charm.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fantasy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a pleasant situation unlikely to happen", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If I won a lot of money, my fantasy would be to travel the world.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to complain", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to say that something is wrong or unsatisfactory", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He always has to complain about never having money.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to associate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to connect someone in your mind with someone or something else", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He seemed to associate her luck with that penny she  always kept on her.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mailbag", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large bag or pouch used in transporting mail in bulk ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He enjoyed reading the interesting letters posted in the Reader Mailbag column.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "In pairs, write down questions about lotteries and winning money.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use hypothetical situation questions as much as possible.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask other classmates your questions and note down their answers.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Go back to your original partner and compare your findings.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make mini-presentations to other groups on your findings.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I can talk about manners, customs and superstitions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can talk about my attitudes toward an action. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can talk about hypothetical situations.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "q